{#
  Tree view (2.24, theme partial `tree`): a navigation tree with disclosures to any depth, following the WAI-ARIA APG
  navigation treeview (ul[role=tree] > li[role=none] > a[role=treeitem] + ul[role=group]). Without JavaScript every
  item is a plain link and the groups the server marked expanded are shown; js/nowo-ui-tree.js (load it on the page:
  it is not in the default `scripts` list) adds the keyboard model, folding, lazy children, moves and drag and drop.
  Slots: tree (root), tree_item (each li), tree_link (the treeitem link), tree_group (child lists).

  Required:
    - nodes: list of hashes {id, label (View\Label|string), href, current?, expanded?, children? (nodes),
      has_children? (true without children: lazy), children_url? (JSON children, see the script), icon? (text, e.g. an
      emoji), badge? (string), link_attr? and item_attr? (2.34: extra attributes of the link / the li, `class` added to
      the slot classes, checked by nowo_ui_safe_attrs(): no on*, style, srcdoc or unsafe URLs; the attributes the
      treeview owns, such as href, role, tabindex, aria-level and the data-nowo-ui-tree-* hooks, stay the partial's)}
    - label (View\Label|string): accessible name of the tree
  Optional:
    - movable (bool): Alt+arrows and drag and drop emit nowo-ui:tree:move / nowo-ui:tree:drop (the host moves)
    - actions_template: template included after each link with {node} (e.g. "+" and "⋯" buttons; give them
      tabindex="-1" and a keyboard shortcut so the tree keeps one tab stop)
    - leading_template (2.34): template included inside the link before the label with {node} (e.g. a check icon: node.icon
      is plain text). It is inside the link: no interactive content
    - attr: root attributes (no on*; attr.id is the tree id that prefixes the group ids), bundle
  The current node's ancestors are always expanded (2.24), so the current item is visible and is the tab stop.
  Lazy children (children_url) are built by the script from JSON: link_attr, item_attr and leading_template apply to
  server-rendered nodes only.
#}
{% set _b = bundle|default(null) %}
{# 2.24: every group id is prefixed with the tree id (attr.id, or a generated one) — unique across trees on a page #}
{% set _tree_id = (attr|default({})).id ?? ('nowo-ui-tree-' ~ random(100000000, 999999999)) %}
<ul class="{{ nowo_ui_class('tree', _b) }}" id="{{ _tree_id }}" role="tree" aria-label="{{ label|nowo_ui_trans }}" data-nowo-ui-tree{% if movable|default(false) %} data-nowo-ui-tree-movable{% endif %}{{ nowo_ui_attrs('tree', _b) }}{{ nowo_ui_html_attrs((attr|default({}))|filter((v, k) => k != 'id')) }}>
    {{ include('@NowoUiKitBundle/partials/_tree_items.html.twig', {tree_id: _tree_id, nodes: nodes, level: 1, tab_first: not nowo_ui_tree_has_current(nodes), actions_template: actions_template|default(null), leading_template: leading_template|default(null), movable: movable|default(false), bundle: _b}, false) }}
</ul>
